Z||000009||80's BOY||07-22-2000||12:29 PM||||i recently raced a guy with a Probe GTX i think it was. (whatever the fastest one is in their own little world.) anyway, we were racing for big money 'cause this guy talks big crap all over town how my paint job is faster than my car. i KILLED him off the line with my 3.1 and had him by a car length all the way up the end of 3rd gear and then he blew by me. my advice, race him for a light to light in front of his friends but don't do a full quarter. you'll lose money like me. everyone was still very impressed that i did so well. he's smoked alot of ricers around here. guess i blew my cover. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||b lo 0||07-24-2000||10:11 AM||||Hey Vinny-I just read the spark plug thread, and, dude, as a friend, that wasn't cool.  I think that if you just apologized everyone would go on with their Fiero driving lives.  We are all here to discuss one of the coolest little cars of all time-the Pontiac Fiero.  If we can discuss the car in a mature, professional manner, maybe we could get more people to love their cars as much as we do (face it, if you didn't like your Fiero, why would you be on this BB?).  What I'm saying is, Fiero owners are a special breed of people, and we deserve the good image bestowed upon us by our continuing faith in our cars and our good manners at shows and on websites alike.  We don't go around saying "This sucks because it's not a Fiero" but instead we say "This is a pretty good car, even if it's not a Fiero." (even if we are thinking 'But my GT would spank this thing in an instant.')  Well, I'm going to shut up now.  Happy Fiero-ing all!!<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car||||reg||1
Z||000011||vinnywolfe||07-24-2000||04:34 PM||||sounds good to me BloO.  <BR>i do apologize that that thread got out of hand.  i went overboard trying to defend a product that i believe in.  anyway i do apologize to anyone that was offended and i am not trying to piss people off when i say that the fiero is not a sports car.  i do think its a great sports car.  i have to plead ignorance on that.  all i have for a driver is an 84 four banger.  <BR>i just finished up my 87gt that i have been working on religiously for a year.  i had never driven it before.  it was towed to where i have been working on it.  anyway i took it out last night for the first time and WOW.  that thing scoots!<BR>anyway, i just found it hypocritical that when i got bent out of shape about spark plugs, everyone told me to settle down. then, when i criticized a product that these people believe in (their cars) they all go balistic on me.<BR>anyway,  i'm not starting that again.<BR>but, when members send me threatening email to my private address, THAT'S GOING TO FAR!  i will stand up for myself and the threads you read (that these people chose to post themselves)have NO place on this forum.  THOSE WERE SENT TO THE MEMBERS PRIVATE EMAIL ADDRESS.  THEY chose to post them.  <BR>i'm not going to open another pandora's box.  again, i apologize to everyone.  and i will chalk this one up under "lessons learned".<BR>i don't feel like arguing.  i'm too damned excited about going and driving my new (well, new to me) FIERO.<P>i am probably going to get many answers to my threads now, but i do enjoy the forum.<P>keep the ideas and suggestions a comin'.<P>later days,<BR>vinny<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000012||StuGood||07-24-2000||06:24 PM||||Vinnywolfe:  Thanks. We (well, I do, anyway) accept your apology   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  From here, let's drive on, with the "curse control" turned ON   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<P>Speaking of driving on, the only thing I know about the Probe GT, is that it's one of the few non-Fiero cars that holds my interest.  There's a purple one parked in the same spot every day where I work, and I admire its looks when I walk by the window.  I always think, "if only it had plastic body panels!" <P>I heard once that common replacement parts for the Probe can be ridiculously expensive, though.  Also, since the Probe is (I think) front wheel drive, does its handling suffer?  Any Probe owners out there have any info to share? <P>P.S. - BTW, Vinnywolfe: Thanks for bringing another Fiero GT back to life  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> !  <P>     <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||14
