Z||000017||Dan86gt3.8||07-25-2000||02:22 PM||||mY friend had an 95 probe gt.  And it was one of the "factory freaks" becase at the track all the other owners even the ones that had all the bolt'on(s)were getting beat ny his. all he did was a dynomax muffler and a cold air kit.  Anyways when I raced him when I had 2.8 liters we were even till about second and then he was gone.  After a little time when buy and I swapped to my 3.8 we raced again from a light and I jumped out to like 2 cars and then he stayed 1 car behind me the whole race and I went to about 100.  So In my opion if both drivers being the same that a probe gt defenitley will beat a 2.8 stock fiero, but if you go slap another liter on the fiero then boom you have a fiero that will beat a porbe.<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>15" konig monsoon's<BR>rear swaybar/ and urethane on rear.<BR>Soon to come urethane all the way around. and new yellow paint w/ raised spoiler!!!!<BR>(also in way future years forced induction on my 3.8!!!!!!!!!)||||reg||1
Z||000018||Fformula88||07-25-2000||04:56 PM||||Assuming all cars are stock, the Probe GT's will beat the Fiero's with 2.8's.  The 93+ GT's have the 2.5L V6, while the 89-92's have a 2.2L SOHC 12V Turbo four.  That engine puts out around 190 Lb-Ft of torque, not sure the HP.  But both are very fast compared to a Fiero.  The Probes, however, have very little aftermarket support.  So it is very difficult and EXPENSIVE to modify them beyond basic exhausts and intake stuff.  So it would be rare that anyone with an engine transplant in their Fiero wouldn't beat one.  <P>As for which is better... the Fiero is hands down more fun to drive.  I have a 97 Probe SE as my daily driver, and its a very nice car.  But it just doesn't give you that road feel and connectedness to the car the Fiero does.||||reg||1
